# What keeps this index the parent-workspace index.
#
# GitNexus reads .gitignore, and until ADR-031 that was enough: the parent
# ignored /BEs/ and the four sibling directories, so `analyze` here saw docs and
# services-status and nothing else. Since the fifteen sub-repos became submodules
# those paths had to leave .gitignore — an ignored path is one `git submodule add`
# refuses — and the very next analyze pulled all fifteen codebases in: 143 files
# and 1651 nodes became 1480 files and 9567 nodes, one index holding the whole
# platform.
#
# This file restores the boundary without touching .gitignore. Each sub-repo has
# its OWN GitNexus index, registered under its own name — see docs/gitnexus.md
# for the registry-name table. Querying the platform's code through
# `fullstack-marketplace-blueprint` is always the wrong index, and this file is
# what stops it from being possible.
#
# ⚠️ Every new sub-repo needs a line here as well as a submodule entry. Verify
# after any analyze: `stats.files` in .gitnexus/meta.json must stay in the low
# hundreds. Thousands means a sub-repo got in.

BEs/
marketplace-admin/
marketplace-nginx/
marketplace-shopowner/
marketplace-user/
